---
// src/components/blog/visuals/SchoolAccommodationsVisual.astro
---

<div class="apple-glass-card apple-specular-top my-10 p-5 sm:p-7 rounded-3xl border border-gray-100 shadow-sm bg-gradient-to-br from-white/95 via-gray-50/50 to-blue-50/20 text-left">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-4">
    <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-brand-navy"></span>
    <h3 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-lg sm:text-xl tracking-tight m-0">
      The 3 Tiers of Neurodivergent School Accommodations (IEP / 504 / EHCP)
    </h3>
  </div>

  <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    When requesting school support across the UK, USA, Australia, or Dubai, general requests ("please be patient") are rejected. Use this 3-tier clinical accommodation framework for meetings:
  </p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 sm:gap-5">
    <!-- Tier 1: Environmental -->
    <div class="bg-white/90 border border-gray-200/80 rounded-2xl p-4 sm:p-5 flex flex-col">
      <span class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-900 bg-blue-100 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full w-fit mb-3">
        Tier 1: Environmental
      </span>
      <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-sm mb-2">Classroom Atmosphere</h4>
      <ul class="text-xs text-gray-700 space-y-2 list-disc pl-4 flex-grow">
        <li>Seating away from high-traffic doors and humming HVAC vents.</li>
        <li>Wobble cushion or sensory band on desk legs.</li>
        <li>Noise-cancelling ear defenders during independent silent work.</li>
        <li>Designated quiet decompression space.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Tier 2: Instructional -->
    <div class="bg-white/90 border border-gray-200/80 rounded-2xl p-4 sm:p-5 flex flex-col">
      <span class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-900 bg-amber-100 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full w-fit mb-3">
        Tier 2: Instructional
      </span>
      <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-sm mb-2">Delivery &amp; Tasks</h4>
      <ul class="text-xs text-gray-700 space-y-2 list-disc pl-4 flex-grow">
        <li>Visual schedules &amp; chunked tasks (1 assignment = 3 sub-steps).</li>
        <li>Provide printed outlines rather than copying off whiteboard.</li>
        <li>Extra 25% time on exams &amp; quiet testing room.</li>
        <li>Visual timers (TimeTimer) rather than verbal countdowns.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Tier 3: Emotional & Behavioral -->
    <div class="bg-white/90 border border-gray-200/80 rounded-2xl p-4 sm:p-5 flex flex-col">
      <span class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-900 bg-emerald-100 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full w-fit mb-3">
        Tier 3: Emotional
      </span>
      <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-sm mb-2">Psychological Safety</h4>
      <ul class="text-xs text-gray-700 space-y-2 list-disc pl-4 flex-grow">
        <li>"Safe Person" pass: discreet card to visit SENCO/nurse.</li>
        <li>No cold-calling for spontaneous reading aloud in class.</li>
        <li>Never taking away recess/break time as punishment for focus issues.</li>
        <li>Secret hand signal to request a 2-minute movement break.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-4 p-3 bg-white/80 rounded-xl border border-gray-200/70 text-xs text-gray-600 text-center">
    📋 <strong>Action Step:</strong> Bring these specific points in writing to your next school meeting rather than debating diagnostic terminology.
  </div>
</div>
